module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.pipe_into_a_declared_function_resolves_as_a_method

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyImpossible }

data pipe_into_a_declared_function_resolves_as_a_method: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "pipe_into_a_declared_function_resolves_as_a_method" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: AtCeiling {
      rung: StructurallyImpossible,
      ceiling_reason: "the pipe has no constructor of its own after the front end: the seed parser builds the direct-call node for each pipe form (v1.compiler.parse pipe_call_expr_data) and v2 body lowering builds the application node (v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_pipe_application), so a pipe head is bound by whatever binds that call head and no route can resolve it as a method because it is a pipe" as NonEmptyStr
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: `x |> f(a)`, where f is a declared function the site can reach by import or in its own module, is resolved as a method `f` on the type of x instead of as the call f(x, a) it abbreviates. Only heads with no declared signature (count, map, filter, a host-registered primitive) existed as methods, so the pipe worked for them and refused for every declared function.",
    "HARM: a loud refusal, not silent wrongness -- the seed reported \"method 'f' not found on receiver type 'Primitive(Int)'\" -- so the cost was authorship time. Every NAMESPACE-XL rename wave had to rewrite pipe sites into direct calls (31 of 38 sites in the join instrument slice, 75 of 85 sort_by sites), and the binding-diff join (#15083) grew a RelocateHeadStep arm to do it; that arm's dissolution trigger is this repair. A witness fixture had to be weakened to avoid the shape (test.claim.dag_parse_continuation_operator_witness, restored by this change).",
    "THE CHAIN (DESIGN 6b), MEASURED ON BOTH PATHS AT 88e8991e557 BEFORE THE REPAIR, each by a binary built from that tree. SEED: the earliest unjustified link is the parser. v1.compiler.parse parse_pipe_rhs built an ExprMethodCall for an unqualified pipe, the node `x.f(a)` builds, so v1.compiler.infer could only ask the receiver's type for a method, while the qualified pipe `x |> a.b.f(a)` already built the node a direct qualified call builds and bound through the kernel. The pipe's meaning was recorded for one of its two forms. v2 (THE AUTHORITY): resolve bound the head correctly -- `f` in `7 |> f(a: true)` resolved to the imported pa.f by declaration identity -- and infer refused the inner application with application_positional_deficit at `f`, because v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_binary_apply lowered the pipe as an opaque infix Transform and gave it its call meaning only for a fold head (fold_call_lowering_piped). So v2 failed one link later than the seed: at lowering, not resolution. v2.extdeps.languages.dag dag_infix_operators carries only the pipe's binding power; its meaning (a call with the left operand first) is stated by the seed parser and by v2's receiver-call lowering, which already lowers `recv.f(a)` to f(recv, a).",
    "THE REPAIR, ONE RULE AT BOTH LINKS (DESIGN 6b root generalization: the two pipe forms in the seed and the fold head in v2 were three leaves of one rule). Seed: v1.compiler.parse pipe_call_expr_data makes the unqualified pipe the ExprCall the direct call f(x, a) builds, with the left operand as the first argument; a declared head then binds through its signature and the direct-call shape walls, and a head with no declared signature keeps the known-method bridge that already serves `count(xs)`. v2: v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_pipe_application makes every non-fold pipe the application its right operand names with the left operand as its first positional actual; v2.std.arrow_signature application_binding_plan then binds it like any application. Seed maintenance under gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing: it serves the v2 self-host program by removing a divergence the rename waves had been paying for.",
    "EVIDENCE, EXECUTED. Seed: test.claim.pipe_into_declared_function_witness is itself the specimen -- it imports test.fixture.pipe_head_provider and pipes into its declarations, so on the pre-repair seed the module refused to resolve and no claim ran; on the repaired seed all four claims pass, including the non-commutative `10 |> sub(a: 3) == 7`, the kernel heads count/map/first and the host-realized list_push, and an undeclared head that still refuses beside its declared control. Measured separately by probe with the same two seeds: an ambiguous imported head refuses with \"ambiguous reference 'twice': 2 candidates\", and an undeclared one with \"function 'nowhere_declared' not found in scope\", both located. v2: v2.test.claim.pipe_application runs resolve, infer_and_discharge and eval over a two-module program: the direct-call control, named, positional, bare and chained pipes evaluate; `true |> f(7)` refuses with application_argument_does_not_inhabit (the left operand fills the first slot); the lowered pipe hashes equal to its direct call; unknown-label and bound-twice refusals reach the piped application; not-found and ambiguous heads refuse at resolve with resolve_reason_unbound_symbol and resolve_reason_ambiguous_symbol.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (a typed, located refusal on both paths; nothing silent). NOW: structurally impossible on both front ends, at the grain of the pipe form -- neither the seed parser nor v2 lowering has a node for a pipe other than the call it abbreviates, so a pipe head is resolved by the one route its call head takes. NOT A CLAIM: that a declared function can never be shadowed by or confused with a kernel method of the same spelling. That is name resolution's question, decided the same way for `count(xs)` and `xs |> count`, and outside this class. Emission targets receive the call node the front end built and were not separately measured for pipe sites.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.parse", decl_name: "pipe_call_expr_data"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_pipe_application"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.pipe_into_declared_function_witness", decl_name: "a_pipe_into_an_imported_declared_function_binds_the_left_operand_first"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.test.claim.pipe_application", decl_name: "a_pipe_into_an_imported_declared_function_evaluates"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.test.claim.pipe_application", decl_name: "the_left_operand_fills_the_first_slot"),
  ],
}
